10515	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s1","entry":{"id":"review-93dfb506a1b018e0114ca6cca6f32040","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:51:41.573Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers s1 acceptance criteria ac1–ac5 without implementing the adjacent tool-family or cutover work.","evidence":"DEF §6.1 requires once-after-success execution for every caller, failure reporting without losing success, no hooks on failures or denials, serial registration order, and agent compatibility. LLD §§2, 5 and 6 address each; §7 explicitly leaves hook registrations to s7. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Preserve this scope.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The executor currently returns the tool result unchanged at the no-schema and checked-success exits, and callTool rebuilds its typed success result.","evidence":"executeTool contains `if (outputSchema === undefined || !result.success) return result;` and `if (dataCheck.ok) return result;`. callTool returns `{ success: true, data: result.data ... , output: result.output }`. ToolDeps.caller is optional with the stated three identities. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Split the combined no-schema/failure branch so failed schema-less calls cannot run hooks.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The hook registry is new; the typed helper, fakeTool factory and approval test seams are available for reuse.","evidence":"Reading the executor, registry and barrel and searching src for registerToolHook, runToolHooks and hookFailures found no existing implementation. call-tool.ts implements the stated generic helper; _fakes.ts supports schema-less tools; executor.ts exports _setApprovalGateForTests and _setCommonApprovalForTests. Analyzer drill-down was attempted but failed with shaper-llm-unavailable and an invalid response-schema error. [files: src/daemon/tools/registry.ts, src/daemon/tools/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/_fakes.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Reuse the existing helper and seams.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The specified hook dispatch contract completely handles the tool names accepted by executeTool.","evidence":"registry.ts documents `Resolve a name to a canonical Tool. Honors aliases.` Its getTool resolves aliases to a Tool with a canonical id. read-only-tool-loop.ts checks `tool.id` but dispatches `execute(name, ...)`, preserving the original alias. The LLD does not specify whether its helper receives the incoming toolId or resolved tool.id, nor test aliases. Using the incoming name would skip canonical hooks for successful alias calls. [files: src/daemon/tools/registry.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Require executor dispatch using resolved tool.id and define canonical registration semantics. Add an alias invocation test proving canonical hooks run exactly once.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The typed helper and agent text consumer require the reporting changes identified by the design.","evidence":"callTool constructs a new success object containing only success, data and output, so it needs explicit hookFailures propagation. The read-only loop constructs tool_result blocks with `content: result.output`, so appended failure lines reach that consumer without changing the loop. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts]","action":"Implement the explicit typed propagation and preserve the existing text consumption path.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The hook addition can preserve existing results without a stored-data migration when no hooks are registered.","evidence":"ToolResult is an execution interface with optional data and failure fields; executeTool currently returns the original result at its success exits. The proposed registry is in memory, matching HLD §6: `Hooks are registered in code at start-up, not stored.` Returning the original object when the failure list is empty preserves the examined consumers' behavior. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md]","action":"Keep hook state transient and omit hookFailures entirely when empty.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The hook stage and optional failure report belong to s1 and do not redesign approval or schema validation.","evidence":"HLD §5.1 assigns s1 the hook registry, registration order, successful checked execution and failure report. §§5.2–5.3 assign output checking and approval to s2 and s3. The proposed callTool field propagation preserves the existing signature and carries s1's report through the existing s2 adapter. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Keep approval policy, schema language and conversion behavior unchanged.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"A shallow frozen copy prevents a hook from changing the result received by the caller.","evidence":"ToolResult.data is `unknown` and can hold nested mutable objects; callTool forwards the same data reference. The LLD promises `A rule cannot change what the caller gets back` while freezing only top-level fields. A Node reproduction with `Object.freeze({...result})` followed by `copy.data.total=9` changed the original result.data.total to 9. This can invalidate data after schema validation. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Give hooks an isolated result snapshot, or explicitly design and enforce deep immutability for supported payloads. Test nested data mutation and mutation followed by a thrown error.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Converting every non-Error thrown value with String(value) guarantees that failure reporting never throws.","evidence":"LLD §5 specifies `anything else String(value)` and promises the report `never throws while being built`. A Node reproduction of `String(Object.create(null))` throws `Cannot convert object to primitive value`. A throwing conversion can escape runToolHooks, stop later hooks, and reach executeTool's outer catch, which returns success:false. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S001/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Guard error-message extraction with its own catch and use a fixed nonempty fallback before truncation. Test null-prototype objects and throwing coercion methods.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.3","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"deps.signal provides a bound on a hook that never settles.","evidence":"ToolHookContext exposes only toolId, input, result and caller, so hooks cannot access deps.signal through the declared contract. executeTool does not race tool execution against cancellation. The read-only loop separately races dispatch against its own args.signal, but this protection is not provided by executeTool or callTool for other callers. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S001/LLD.md]","action":"State accurately that the hook stage has no cancellation bound, or design explicit signal propagation and cancellation behavior. Distinguish caller abandonment from stopping the hook.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream s1 acceptance criterion maps to planned tests using existing test infrastructure.","evidence":"DEF §6.1 has five criteria, and LLD §6 maps all five to concrete proposed hook tests. The existing approval-class-mapping test checks each snapshot tool remains registered with an identical input schema and asserts the snapshot contains 228 tools. The fakeTool helper and approval seams support the proposed executor cases. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S001/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/_fakes.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Retain this mapping and add alias dispatch, nested mutation and hostile thrown-value cases to cover the identified gaps. These are planned tests, not verified implementation results.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":4,"med":0,"low":7,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T13:51:41.573Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
