8252	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s1","entry":{"id":"review-f71c3a08418cd946d5da0bb14d9ae134","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:54:11.519Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers Story s1's five acceptance criteria and keeps actual tracker-hook registration in s7.","evidence":"DEF §6.1 requires successful-call hooks, failure reporting without changing success, exclusion of failed/denied calls, serial registration order, and compatibility. The proposed executor stage and acceptance mapping address all five. HLD §5.7 assigns caller cutover to s7; this design registers no production rules. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md]","action":"Preserve this scope during implementation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The executor currently returns the tool's own result through two success paths, after any applicable output check.","evidence":"Read executeTool in full: `if (outputSchema === undefined || !result.success) return result;` and `if (dataCheck.ok) return result;`. Approval denial, input rejection and output mismatch return earlier or separately. The first return also handles failed results, so its replacement must retain that distinction. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Split the combined no-schema/failure branch so failed results never reach hooks.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"callTool currently rebuilds successful results and would discard a new hookFailures field without adaptation.","evidence":"The full helper returns `{ success: true, data: result.data as Static<T['outputSchema']>, output: result.output }`; TypedToolResult's success variant declares only those three fields. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts]","action":"Add and conditionally copy hookFailures as designed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The hook registry is new, while canonical alias resolution and the stated optional caller identity already exist.","evidence":"Source search found no ToolHook, registerToolHook, runToolHooks or hookFailures implementation. Read registry.ts: getTool resolves direct ids first, then aliasToId to the canonical Tool. ToolDeps declares `caller?: 'agent' | 'daemon' | 'workflow' | undefined`. The analyzer was attempted but failed with a planning-schema error; source reads supplied the verification. [files: src/daemon/tools/registry.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Key execution by the resolved tool.id and retain optional caller handling.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The executor, shared result type, typed adapter and public registration export are the necessary integration points described by this design.","evidence":"Read executor.ts, types.ts, call-tool.ts and index.ts. Execution converges in executeTool; ToolResult is defined in types.ts; callTool projects the result; index.ts is the tools barrel. The read-only loop dispatches through executeTool and puts `result.output` into tool_result content, so appended failure text reaches that consumer without a new loop-side field handler. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/index.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts]","action":"Implement the listed changes and leave the text-consuming loop unchanged.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"This story needs no stored-record migration, and its absent-by-default report can preserve existing result behavior.","evidence":"HLD §6 explicitly says hooks are registered in startup code and are not stored. ToolResult and TypedToolResult currently contain no hook report. The executor returns original result objects on success; the design preserves that path when no failure report is added and introduces no persisted hook shape. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts]","action":"Verify property absence and result identity, as planned; do not emit hookFailures with an empty array.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed shared-contract refinements have been reconciled with the effective upstream contracts.","evidence":"HLD sc1 sketches a required caller and mutable HookFailure[] report; this LLD explicitly changes caller to allow undefined and uses readonly reports. It also extends s2-owned TypedToolResult. Reviewed amendment records AMD-1 through AMD-7: they address sc2–sc5, with no sc1 amendment or approval resolving the refinements acknowledged in this LLD's open questions. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-6.json]","action":"Record whether these are accepted sketch refinements or require a shared-contract amendment, including the additive sc2 result field.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The stated cancellation limitation matches current execution: the executor and typed helper do not bound the tool promise, while the read-only loop bounds only its own wait.","evidence":"Read executeTool and callTool in full: both await execution without a cancellation race. The read-only loop uses `untilAborted(dispatch(call.name, call.input), args.signal)`; untilAborted rejects its wrapper on abort and leaves the underlying work running. The design explicitly identifies a never-settling hook as undetected and specifies a pre-hook log for diagnosis. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts]","action":"Retain this explicit limitation and the pre-hook log; do not imply cancellation stops hook execution.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every s1 acceptance criterion maps to a proposed test, and the reused fixtures and compatibility check support those tests.","evidence":"Compared DEF §6.1 with the design's mapping: ac1–ac5 each have explicit proving subjects. Read _fakes.ts: fakeTool supports schema and no-schema results. The executor exports both named approval seams. Read approval-class-mapping.test.ts: it asserts the 228-entry snapshot and compares every original tool id and input schema. These are design-time test plans, not evidence that new hook tests already pass. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/_fakes.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Implement the mapped tests, including approval-before-hook ordering, then run the listed regression suites.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":9,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T13:54:11.519Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
